SCREENS BBS-ROUTES
HELP a add  Enter edit  Del remove  +/- order  R re-run  ? guide
KEY a Adds a rule.
KEY Enter Edits the rule.
KEY Del Removes it (asks first).
KEY + Moves it up. The first rule that matches wins.
KEY - Moves it down.
KEY R Runs the rules again over unprocessed traffic (shows the count first).
SEE BBS-SETUP BBS-GUARD
BEGIN_TEXT
Each rule matches a routing indicator, part of one, or a call with a
wildcard (UHE*), and names the route, the ALE addresses to call in order,
the key, a schedule, and whether to compress.

Routed traffic keys the radio only while machine mode and routing are
both on. Calling the ALE addresses is the radio's job; this screen only
lists them.
END
